Active phase: Apex GUI Phase 01 - Core Forge Shell
Newest base used: ApexUI_phase_1_base_3.tar
Patch scope: promote disabled action behavior from response-only coverage into the visible starter shell

What changed:
- Added disabled quiet button/action APIs to ApexUi.
- Added a disabled Settings action to the demo top bar.
- Kept disabled Settings action inert; ApexResponse still prevents disabled actions from emitting.
- Updated the Phase 01 semantic snapshot and golden to include the disabled Settings action.
- Added semantic test coverage for the disabled Settings action entry.
- Updated the active Phase 01 plan with a base_3 adjustment note and a pending operator check for the visible disabled action.

What is now real:
- The demo shell shows a disabled top-bar action as a real Apex API path, not a hidden unit-test-only behavior.
- App/demo code still uses Apex APIs for the primary UI path.
- Disabled responses cannot activate, cannot report pressed, and cannot emit actions.
- Accepted starter shell semantics now include top-bar disabled-action structure.

What remains placeholder/unsupported:
- Operator has not yet accepted the visible disabled Settings action feel for this patch.
- Keyboard traversal and accessibility are still not claimed beyond egui-exposed focus state used by button painting.
- The raw egui escape hatch exists on ApexFrame but is not used by the demo primary path.
- Density exists as a starter token and only affects button height so far.
- Visual screenshot goldens remain deferred until the operator wants a visual lock lane.
- Phase 01 seal docs/Rustdoc remain pending until the operator explicitly closes the phase.

